# Stage2_LiftUpdate's arrival at the top (ruling 5, 2), at its first call (the lift scene running,
# its V-int object installed): the map scroll 1/16 px above the top with the lift at full speed
# up, so this frame's move takes g_MapScrollY negative: Stage2_LiftArriveTop (the boss arena and
# the boss), Shake_Start and the three clears. The real game reaches it once per lift ride (TAS
# f32065, fuzz-30600/34200): verify samples those calls out (a call after an entry's 2000th is
# compared 1 in 64, and an entry gets no probe for new instructions), so a case pins it.

case arrive
l $FFFFE00E = $00001000
l $FFFFE006 = $FFFF0000
l $FFFFDFFE = $FFFF0000
